# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/
bin/
work/

# Built binaries (repo-root only — an unanchored pattern here would also
# match, and silently git-ignore, the cmd/pentakit/ source directory and
# everything ever added to it since; `bin/` above already covers `make build`'s
# actual output, this guards only a stray `go build -o pentakit ./cmd/main`
# run from the repo root)
/pentakit
/pentakit-*
# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
.bin/